IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dc-tanf`

-- District of Columbia TANF -- worked cases from the seat of the applicant or recipient. Every assertion is a claim about the
-- ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The deductions the Mayor sets by rule are HYPOTHETICAL inputs (a $160 work
-- expense deduction, a $200 earned income disregard), not the DCMR figures. Expected results were worked by hand; the payment
-- level is the 1998 s 4-205.52(c) figure unless a case says otherwise. Family of 3: standard payment level $712, level of
-- assistance $379.

§ `Cases`

§§ `The standards`

#ASSERT `What are the DC TANF standards for my family` 3 EQUALS `answered` (`DC standards` OF 712, 379)
#ASSERT `What are the DC TANF standards for my family` 19 EQUALS `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2786, 1482)
#ASSERT `What are the DC TANF standards for my family` 20 EQUALS `not covered` `the s 4-205.52(c) table stops at a family of 19`

§§ `The payment`

-- No income: $379.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 TRUE 0 0 0 0 TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 379
-- No income, with a current level of assistance of $900 (HYPOTHETICAL, after the (d-1) inflation increases): $900.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 TRUE 0 0 0 0 TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE 900 EQUALS `answered` 900
-- An applicant earning $600: gross 600, not over 712; after the $160 work expense, 440, not over 712; countable 600 - 160 - 200 =
-- 240; payment 379 - 240 = $139.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 TRUE 600 0 0 0 TRUE 160 0 200 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 139
-- Earning $800: gross income over $712: not eligible (s 4-205.10(a)).
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 800 0 0 0 TRUE 160 0 200 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- An adult earning $500 and a student child $300: gross income is "total earned income", 800, over 712: not eligible, although
-- s 4-205.11(a)(4) would leave the child's earnings out of the payment (finding 3).
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 500 300 0 0 TRUE 160 0 200 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- The same adult earning $500 and the child $100: gross 600 passes; the child's $100 is disregarded; countable 500 - 160 - 200 =
-- 140; payment $239.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 500 100 0 0 TRUE 160 0 200 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 239
-- Child support $400 in September 2025: the first $150 disregarded, 250 counted: $129. From October 2025: all disregarded: $379.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 0 0 0 400 FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 129
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 0 0 0 400 TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 379
-- Unearned $375: a check of $4, under $10: nothing paid (s 4-205.51).
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 0 0 375 0 TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- Earnings $300 in a month the disregards are withheld (a late report): all 300 counted: $79.
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 3 FALSE 300 0 0 0 TRUE 160 0 200 TRUE 0 EQUALS `answered` 79
#ASSERT `How much DC TANF would we get` 20 FALSE 0 0 0 0 TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the s 4-205.52(c) table stops at a family of 19`

§§ `s 4-205.11(a)(3) -- the initial applicant's test`

-- An initial applicant with $720 unearned income: over the $712 standard: ineligible. A recipient with the same: the test does
-- not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`the family passes the s 4-205.11(a)(3) applicant test` (`DC family month` OF 3, TRUE, 0, 0, 720, 0, TRUE, 0, 0, 0, FALSE) (`DC standards` OF 712, 379))
#ASSERT `the family passes the s 4-205.11(a)(3) applicant test` (`DC family month` OF 3, FALSE, 0, 0, 720, 0, TRUE, 0, 0, 0, FALSE) (`DC standards` OF 712, 379)

§§ `s 4-205.11a -- 60 months`

#ASSERT `Can we keep getting federally funded TANF` 59 EQUALS `federally funded TANF may continue: fewer than 60 counted months`
#ASSERT `Can we keep getting federally funded TANF` 60 EQUALS `federally funded TANF may continue only if the Mayor exempts the unit for hardship or battering or extreme cruelty (s 4-205.11a(e))`

§§ `Deadlines and notices`

-- Received 2 March 2026: 45 days: 16 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the agency act on my application` (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS Date 16 4 2026
-- It became clear on 1 June 2026 that the child will be away more than 90 days: the 5-day period is 1 to 5 June.
#ASSERT `By when must I report my child's absence` (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS Date 5 6 2026
-- Postmarked 1 May for 16 May: 15 days: timely. For 15 May: 14 days: not. With a s 4-205.55(b) case: timely anyway.
#ASSERT `Was the notice timely` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 16 5 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the notice timely` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Was the notice timely` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) TRUE
-- Hearing asked for on 10 May, before the 16 May effective date: assistance continues.
#ASSERT `Will my TANF continue during the hearing` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 16 5 2026) TRUE (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS `assistance continues unchanged until the hearing decision (s 4-205.59(a))`
-- An untimely notice postmarked 12 May for 14 May; hearing asked for on 20 May, 8 days after the postmark: reinstated in 96 hours.
#ASSERT `Will my TANF continue during the hearing` (Date 12 5 2026) (Date 14 5 2026) FALSE (Date 20 5 2026) EQUALS `assistance must be reinstated within 96 hours of my request (s 4-205.59(c))`
-- The same untimely notice, hearing asked for on 30 June: heard, but no continued benefits.
#ASSERT `Will my TANF continue during the hearing` (Date 12 5 2026) (Date 14 5 2026) FALSE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS `the hearing is held, but the disputed benefits do not continue (s 4-205.59(d))`
-- 90 days from a 1 May 2026 postmark: 30 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Until when may I ask for a hearing` (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS Date 30 7 2026

§§ `The rules traced`

#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the 45 days to decide an application` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Mayor` `approve or disapprove the application` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Mayor, "no first payment or notice of ineligibility within 45 days of receipt ..." (day 46)
#TRACE `the 45 days to decide an application` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Mayor` DOES `approve or disapprove the application` AT 46
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the 5 days to report a child's long absence` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the parent, guardian or caretaker` `notify the Mayor of the child's absence` 4)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the parent, guardian or caretaker, "the child's absence of more than 90 days not reported ..." (day 5)
#TRACE `the 5 days to report a child's long absence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the parent, guardian or caretaker` DOES `notify the Mayor of the child's absence` AT 5
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the 15 days to answer information from another source` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `present additional information or request a fair hearing` 12)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the 15 days to answer information from another source` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the duty to report a change immediately` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `notify the Mayor of the change` 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
